From 9176be2a800c27443770c8f355bcc888ce769e3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WS-P <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:51:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] redfin: PSCI CPU_SUSPEND power collapse for CPUs 1-7
 (sweetidle=1)

cpu_idle() calls PSCI CPU_SUSPEND 0x40000003 instead of WFI when the next
timer is beyond the lpm-levels minimum residency; resume through XNU's
resume_idle_cpu/arm_init_idle_cpu path plus GIC CPU interface and timer
restore. Frame 0 of the arm,armv7-timer-mem block is the broadcast timer
(SPI 8 on CPU0). Default off; a PSCI error turns it off.
---
 bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c       |   8 +-
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetCPU.cpp |   2 +
 osfmk/arm/arm_init.c          |   7 +
 osfmk/arm64/cpu.c             | 265 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 pexpert/arm/pe_fiq.c          |  14 ++
 5 files changed, 295 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

